{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-action--8","attack-action--9","attack-action--10","attack-action--11","attack-action--12","attack-action--13","attack-action--14","attack-condition--1","instance--18acb1e8-0dbc-5fdc-aa7a-664a37ff2675","instance--d56a57e1-38ee-5115-bcad-e7817668513c","instance--ff8882dc-12bb-5d7f-a769-b6d7c321c8c7","instance--fbe5dafa-8864-524c-b765-e813b0a87575","file--3","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--057c9c6b-5f9d-5a42-a700-338d5f0eb74a","instance--7e8c9301-c3f8-55e9-8894-e81f1b6203d9","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--3622ace1-abf1-5f6e-a5de-a6f584dc1f66","instance--56b40d44-cc57-5e8b-b320-779a685089fd","instance--895aab9a-87c3-51d8-91f8-cc3f6dd1a5a5","instance--3bb881aa-a5ab-51ba-b53d-89d26964ce7d","instance--be99ba49-e121-58a8-ba7b-dd3de316cfcf","instance--57bd700a-faa2-5f72-95f2-2694bcea17c9","instance--c075f5c6-95e8-5553-8f7e-b432b96021c7","instance--3b404379-7d7e-5278-b499-6ac12ee4e90f","instance--5824580a-ff0f-5565-bba6-97a7c9ed3a5e","instance--13a1d2ce-b971-5f8d-952e-3b059edcaebb","instance--87fa4a6b-4596-5860-918e-e16f74da32fa","instance--a16e1ef6-00fd-5f84-9d14-12c26b402614","instance--286ae2b5-dd65-59c2-808e-f0dd99d4271c","instance--e1779b23-a9ed-5f5e-a133-3dff7d2cb0f4"],"properties":[["name","APT31 Jian exploitation flow for CVE-2017-0005"],["description","The report describes how APT31 used a multi-staged packer and reflective loading chain to execute the Jian exploit for CVE-2017-0005."],["scope","incident"],["author",[["name","Eyal Itkin"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","research.checkpoint.com"],["url","https://research.checkpoint.com/2021/the-story-of-jian/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Ship exploit DLL"],["description","Jian, the exploit of CVE-2017-0005, was shipped in a DLL named . It contained an interesting PDB path suggesting that it was written in 2015 under a project named \u201crundll32_getadmin\u201d."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1574.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Invoke AddByGod export"],["description","Speaking of the export directory, the DLL has a single exported function named \u201cAddByGod\u201d, which, as we will learn soon, is the entry function of the packer."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1129"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Decrypt second stage"],["description","The decryption routine is very straightforward. The packer starts by allocating memory for the encrypted code and copies it to the newly allocated buffer. It then allocates a buffer with protection to store the decrypted code. After the buffers are allocated, the packer checks if a string argument, which will be used as a decryption key, was passed to the function. Next, the packer uses the AES256 algorithm with a SHA1 derived key of the passed argument to decrypt the encrypted code. If the decryption is successful, the decrypted code is executed and a second stage payload runs."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Resolve export dynamically"],["description","The second stage begins with a typical shellcode technique, searching the module\u2019s header for the address of and dynamically retrieving a pointer to the export function."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1027"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Decompress PE and jump"],["description","Next, the program decompresses another Portable Executable (PE) and jumps to its entry point."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1140"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Reflectively load embedded executable"],["description","The decompressed PE, which is the 3rd stage in the loading sequence, has intentionally corrupted headers. It does basic loading operations and then begins with a reflective loading of an embedded executable (yes, another one). The loaded PE is the last stage in the loading sequence and is responsible for executing the exploit."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1620"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Collect OS version context"],["description","The exploit creates a rich version context that includes multiple fields, each representing a different characteristic of the target\u2019s operating system."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1082"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Bootstrap GDI and display"],["description","While the initialization phase of this exploit is longer and involves a lot of GDI-related bootstrapping ( , finding the wanted Display, etc.), the actual flow that hijacks the control flow is relatively simple."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0042","technique":"T1587.004"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Register user-mode callback"],["description","After the bootstrap is finished, the exploit triggers a call to the syscall. This initiates a chain of events in the Windows kernel and eventually passes the flow back to our user-mode callback ( ) registered by our UMPD."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1574"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Allocate user-mode object"],["description","Our function allocates a new using , whose sole purpose is to allow UMPD implementations to allocate themselves an and couple it with a . As a direct result, it also means that the is allocated in , using . Storing it in user-mode means that we can access it and craft the struct\u2019s content."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1068"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6b7baffd-afaf-5472-9af2-a263119a77ef","120":"instance--83f38e63-e29a-53f4-99d9-927a195c453f","150":"instance--3e720145-b7a1-5bd6-8a7d-bb13519675d1","180":"instance--bdce060f-d96c-5b06-b8f4-1ab1527fd01d","210":"instance--a4feb251-e6e3-5680-a712-d59c92f73ccf","240":"instance--9a564ca6-b753-5b06-880c-b3aac25c1e73","270":"instance--76861a89-f006-5e0d-8c5b-ebdcb5e926dc","30":"instance--cf41e64d-4a4b-58d9-9962-72d278b2c489","300":"instance--ac1d6edd-482f-5f13-9348-b605afcc260c","330":"instance--ed78dfa1-f300-564f-b2cd-6c99552b9a68","60":"instance--979accb3-1b3e-5af4-9182-78392cbaf904","90":"instance--ae721c42-320e-5ea4-9c77-339a05b6e12f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--11","properties":[["name","Forge fake GDI objects"],["description","And so, the attackers corrupted the to point at a set of fake GDI objects that were forged on a local stack buffer inside the callback."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1068"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--f1e35721-7ac2-54fe-bcf6-5456d2faeaa3","120":"instance--3ff6777e-fcba-5b31-bf0f-3ddf77f6030d","150":"instance--cc6192f9-21a5-5d1a-b954-6a52d989b82d","180":"instance--62a87260-0181-5f49-bc05-733216e4d822","210":"instance--2f2d05c5-8e60-5ac2-b7af-e03027d67957","240":"instance--79c1ec18-d792-5d3d-a7bc-d94fe8b124cf","270":"instance--a035d357-e930-5d33-ab8d-d0314092d036","30":"instance--3af551b8-f6ac-5f54-9f6d-403fecdc69eb","300":"instance--298b5d2a-bf93-51e9-b052-19ce36114a5d","330":"instance--c8ea0da0-a19a-5766-b0d1-8524844a59d1","60":"instance--a204f87d-ace7-5a9e-b3d1-13202bdc5c7b","90":"instance--fff4de11-3f84-52c8-bb77-192210612a62"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--12","properties":[["name","Point palette to shellcode"],["description","To hijack the control flow, the attackers chose to use a Palette and crafted it so that points to their shellcode, exactly as Microsoft pointed out in their blog on the caught-in-the-wild exploit."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1574"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--cac05670-e90e-512c-99cc-c0adf909c3ef","120":"instance--43922820-ddd3-5742-a88d-49c20f8e3fd5","150":"instance--884271a6-8d7b-5c96-9ece-61be4126898b","180":"instance--373a94ef-653d-5c24-96f7-d0cf326d3aea","210":"instance--e58b782a-e75e-5141-bdf0-6d47dbed96bd","240":"instance--5960e46a-3307-5101-b96f-f1bae10e323d","270":"instance--a5ae1125-6ca5-54f1-b9d3-0091a0a38367","30":"instance--e7c521dd-fe09-528b-bb67-1ec53389b876","300":"instance--582e0864-cb5c-5de1-b6c0-e162ae91e8bc","330":"instance--3d5550f3-3e33-5d71-b71e-db2a0a957e5e","60":"instance--b83fc757-0bd4-5b63-a13e-e5b8ef5956d2","90":"instance--2a745819-837b-5585-a366-81a34117a6e5"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--13","properties":[["name","Call syscall to trigger bug"],["description","After everything is built, the callback invokes the syscall with a parameter of . This specific syscall was chosen because of two key features:\n\nThe user passes to it a .\n\nA value of means the kernel directly accesses the user-controlled from within the supplied .\n\nMore specifically, a Stream is extracted from the fully-controlled and is forwarded on to , causing the unsuspecting kernel function to use our fully crafted Stream."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1068"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--2accaaf8-d071-542e-9a10-06866a96b394","120":"instance--75ef5b2f-7c71-566e-baf2-29f54ced8138","150":"instance--73017f0a-a5f3-5dca-b91c-a2d37bcfe21b","180":"instance--2f1b6e5f-d3b0-59e5-b3c8-6c1399d1ce2a","210":"instance--c7aedd91-3346-5b75-9e3a-842851881a25","240":"instance--2146989b-d8a2-53f0-8a1c-cd3d976227e9","270":"instance--1b0bbd91-fa2a-5897-96d0-9e5918961c9c","30":"instance--e6b73353-364e-5586-a07b-e1fdc92ad2d3","300":"instance--0fdc5473-d5b9-5fed-91a3-21958da6287b","330":"instance--fd1cd9e0-5761-5725-801f-bf88b65914e8","60":"instance--a58b8357-6abc-58d7-ad2b-bec48fffcd9b","90":"instance--e8daf33f-0240-5544-9f99-3be7ac96fc1d"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--14","properties":[["name","Execute shellcode in kernel flow"],["description","This chain of functions gradually uses all of the GDI objects that we\u2019ve crafted in our user-mode callback, eventually leading to . This last function invokes our crafted function pointer, thus hijacking the control flow and triggering the execution of our shellcode."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0004","technique":"T1068"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","in